From 992cb8c617fbcdff2cbd4871367b6442ea56dd56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:31:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Request Increased Memory Limit for free teams' App IDs

When an app asks for com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
and the team is free, updateFeatures drops the capability, because
updateAppId.action cannot enable it for free teams. Ask for it through
SideSign's enableCapabilities before downloading the provisioning
profile, so that the profile, and then the signed app, carry the
entitlement. A failure is logged and the app is still installed, with
the default memory limit.

SideStore's additional entitlements, which it adds to every app's own,
give the key the entitlement itself for a value, never true: any value
but false asks for the capability, as updateFeatures reads them. Up to
Cartouche 0.12.1, this asked only for the value true, and so never sent
the request.

Fixes SideStore#1616 for free accounts. Needs the SideSign patch that
adds enableCapabilities.

